+## 6. Concrete proposed live limits — approval pending, NOT RUN
+
+Historical ~40 minutes/~90 MB/194 routes are estimates, not enforcement. The following ceilings are an **engineering proposal for Tony’s build approval**, within the existing one-smoke/two-full-run count; no live permission is granted here. If insufficient, stop with partial evidence and request Tony’s explicit new allocation, never extend automatically.
+
+| Allocation | Intentional HTTP dispatch cap (redirect hops count) | Hard wall-clock / transfer caps | Disk and document limits |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| CHK, one shared Capture smoke | 120 total; reserve/report bootstrap + discovery + REST + any redirect hops; no separate media HEAD in this smoke (`--no-media-head`), capability proved locally | 1800 s total from browser start, including waits/finalization; document worker ≤180 s retaining 90000 ms page timeout/3 s/image wait; browser read/HEAD ≤30 s | 10 distinct document captures total including origin bootstrap; `--limit 10 --skip-prepare --no-media-head`; 100,000,000 persisted bytes including raw/logs/reserve, no pack |
+| E2 run A | 1200 total across all deliberate streams/hops; all declared collections/pagination attempted until complete or bound/stop | 7200 s total including waits/finalization; same per-operation caps | No arbitrary route truncation for a successful full-run claim; bound triggers partial/stopped. Raw ≤150,000,000 bytes; source run plus required pack/raw copies, reports and offline Prepare repeat ≤500,000,000 bytes |
+| E2 run B | Same independent 1200 cap; starts ≥3600 s after A finishes, no automatic restart if A refused/stopped | Same 7200 s total | Same caps; new immutable run and packs |
+
+Campaign ceiling proposed: **2520 intentional dispatches, one smoke + two full attempts**, not browser event counts. Two full-run success/reproducibility remains AC-040, not guaranteed by spending budget. Any first refusal/challenge ends collection and blocks further live allocations in this automatic campaign pending Tony decision. Raw storage 150 MB×3 (run+two pack copies for AC-032) leaves 50 MB for derived/log/evidence within 500 MB; fail early if the actual planned copy would exceed remaining quota. Temporary/partial writes count too. Never delete old outputs to create space.
+
+Planned enforced options/config fields (not existing CLI flags): `--max-operations`, `--max-seconds`, existing `--max-bytes` with explicit scope, plus raw/aggregate storage budget records. Exact CHK planned invocation: `venv/bin/python -m recon_pipeline --project CyberizeGroup --url https://cyberizegroup.com --limit 10 --skip-prepare --no-media-head --max-operations 120 --max-seconds 1800 --max-bytes 100000000`. E2 planned invocation for each distinct run: same project/site without smoke flags, `--max-operations 1200 --max-seconds 7200 --max-bytes 150000000`, aggregate 500,000,000-byte guard for that run’s packs/evidence. These commands are proposals, **not runnable product features today**; E1 must bind shipped help/docs exactly before use.
+
+Admission enforcement: reserve an operation token before dispatch (initial and every redirect); monotonic deadline checked before/after pacing and during waits; byte/file writes reserve quota before committing. Navigation/process supervisor cancels browser at deadline (allow finalization by reserving the last 30 s, not by exceeding total ceiling); read uses AbortSignal and outer timeout. A 10 MiB per-intentional-response decoded-body cap proposed: stream read/count chunks before saving; crossing it aborts and preserves available bytes as explicitly incomplete, stops collection, never calls it a complete response. Historical ArrayBuffer helper buffered fully; the proposed Response.body ReadableStream accumulation is an explicit API refinement at the same decoded-entity boundary, not a client fallback, and must be locally proved. Background resource transfer volume is **not** represented as capped wire bytes; no separate body harvesting. Runtime browser cache/temp storage is monitored separately and is not equated to saved evidence bytes; resource issues stop, never silently spend more allocation.
