+## 7. Precommit evidence → Tony’s exact candidate → QA reuse
+
+Before every engineering check/live collection, record read-only `git branch --show-current`, `git rev-parse HEAD`, `git status --porcelain=v1 --untracked-files=all`, and `git diff --binary HEAD -- <scoped inputs>` (stored locally, no secrets). More importantly, create a sorted **source identity inventory** over every actual product/test/fixture/config/requirements/governing input used, including untracked files: relative path, byte SHA-256, size, executable bit, symlink target/type. Record declared exclusions (runtime/cache/output/evidence), no broad exclusion of untracked implementation. Freeze one writer; hash before and after checks and reject source drift. Record commands, runtime/browser binary identity, fixture facts, dependency locks and all evidence digests; run metadata stores inventory digest/base HEAD/dirty=true. No fictitious future commit SHA.
